From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kaimrdzt <kaimrdzt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 54/54] LOCAL: arm64: dts: meson-gxl: add S905L3-B TV boxes

Add device trees for two common Amlogic S905L3-B (GXLX2) set-top boxes so
Lakka AMLGX box images can boot them from SD/USB:

- Skyworth E900V22E (1 GiB RAM, MT7668 SDIO WiFi)
- MBH M302A (2 GiB RAM, MT7668 SDIO WiFi)

Both boards are based on the community device trees maintained by ophub
for mainline-based Armbian builds (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT), adapted for the
Lakka 6.18 kernel and extended with:

- a GXLX2 hdmi_tx node using the new amlogic,meson-gxlx2-dw-hdmi
  compatible (directly mapped DesignWare/TOP registers at 0xda800000,
  GXL PHY values) instead of the incorrect meson-g12a-dw-hdmi fallback
- 24 MHz assigned rates for the SD/eMMC input clocks
- MT7668 SDIO WiFi child nodes
- disabled top GPU OPPs the fixed regulators on these boxes cannot reach

S905L3-B boards ship with 1 GiB RAM on several variants; the AMLGX
kernel enlarges the GX CMA pool to 896 MB which does not fit comfortably
in 1 GiB. The Amlogic boot scripts gained an optional cma= uEnv variable
to shrink the pool at boot time for such boards (see
projects/Amlogic/README.md).

Based-on-work-by: ophub <68696949+ophub@users.noreply.github.com>
